ot of money going to poland to  restructure its  economy we're talking about uh more than  one quarter of polish gdp that it will  get in support  from the european union and i think  there is there are so many benefits in  this because  you know you will create new jobs uh for  people who are now working in the coal  mining industry there are huge  opportunities poland is a country with a  tremendous amount of engineers and we  will be needing engineers in this  economy that's coming with hydrogen with  the circular economy  and all these new technologies that will  be applied and these are huge  opportunities  but of course the transition is going to  be extremely complicated for everyone  this is going to be very very  complicated time ahead of us  but the alternative doing nothing is  going to create many more problems than  actually acting well yes and it's  interesting you say that it's going to  be very complicated for everyone because  you've actually said before haven't you  that decarbonization  needs a tectonic shift in the way  society is structured  do you think that national politicians  are being honest enough  with their people about how their lives  are going to change and how soon  well you know i i've been in politics  for over 30 years i've  i've been a national politician been  elected to my national parliament for  six  six times so so i have some experience  and and it's always difficult  uh to confront uh your electorate with  very very difficult messages  especially you know we're in a pandemic  we people are suffering so much and then  you have to tell them  by the way we have a couple of other  crises that are actually  life-threatening that we need to address  um but i think we ca we can't afford the  luxury  of not telling the truth um you know i i  don't want to  to to see my children and my children's  children asking themselves  well our grandparents knew this was  happening why didn't they act  we can't afford to do that and honestly  i believe that  you know we're also in an industrial  revolution these changes are tectonic  and we need to shape them this is the  time for politics this is a time  that society needs to take its own  destiny its own hands  if we just let it happen then the happy  few will come out  stronger and and the large majority of  the population  will suffer if we if we shape it if we  take  initiatives if we change our society  into a sustainable way  that we can make sure that we leave no  one behind i think that that's the  that's the huge task we we  face but it's feasible it is feasible  so what do those changes look like for  individuals  how will their lives change because  obviously some jobs are going to go  aren't they i mean people might  be encouraged to get around very  differently they might be encouraged to  eat very differently  what do you think those changes look  like for individuals  well our lives will change whether we  adapt to climate change or we don't  because if we don't and climate change  the temperature will go  above uh two degrees in increase  and then uh you know the weather  patterns will be more erratic  we will have more firestorms we'll have  more droughts etc  and that will have a huge impact on our  lives if we let that happen  our children will fight wars over water  and food  so we need to change but the change  doesn't have to be  ah doesn't have to take away the value  of our life it will increase the value  of our life  when we change when we change the way we  move around when we  when we eliminate uh combustion engines  and go to electric vehicles  we will have cleaner air in in in our  cities  we will have more safety on our roads uh  when we change the way we eat and we're  more conscious of what we eat  we will reduce the risk of of ecocide of  biodiversity  um disappearing when we go to a circular  economy  we will reduce massively our waste and  we will do something about what david  attenborough has been teaching us  from the beginning and that is taking  away all this plastic waste  out of the oceans if we don't change  there will be more plastic in the oceans  than fish  50 years from now so the changes is a  positive change  of course it will be difficult bloody  difficult honestly speaking  it would be very difficult but just i i  just don't want  people to un to to underestimate the  negative consequences of not acting  uh and i believe that uh acting will  take us to a society  that we can we can truthfully hand over  to our children and grandchildren in a  good conscience  uh saying that we set the uh a world  on a track that will allow humanity to  live within the boundaries of the planet  we've never learned to live within the  boundaries of the planet we need to  learn it now
 

